The rule is recoloring the uniform divider column too — any fully uniform row or column becomes 2.

```python
def transform(grid):
    H = len(grid)
    W = len(grid[0])
    out = [list(r) for r in grid]
    for i in range(H):
        if len(set(grid[i])) == 1:
            out[i] = [2] * W
    for j in range(W):
        col = {grid[i][j] for i in range(H)}
        if len(col) == 1:
            for i in range(H):
                out[i][j] = 2
    return out
